{"name":"Blonde Shell","hex":"#f6edcd","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blonde","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of blond (“person with fair hair”).","Alternative form of blond (“color”)"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of blond.","Stupid, ignorant, naive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blonde"},{"term":"shell","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard external covering of an animal.\nThe calcareous or chitinous external covering of mollusks, crustaceans, and some other invertebrates.","The calcareous or chitinous external covering of mollusks, crustaceans, and some other invertebrates."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the outer covering or shell of something.","To bombard, to fire projectiles at, especially with artillery."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shell"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blond","blocks":[{"text":"Blond or blonde, also referred to as fair hair, is a human hair color characterized by low levels of eumelanin, the dark pigment. The resultant visible hue depends on various factors, but always has some yellowish color. The color can be from the very pale blond to reddish \"strawberry\" blond or golden-brownish (\"sandy\") blond colors. Occasionally, the state of being blond, and specifically the occurrence of blond traits in a predominantly dark or colored population are referred to as blondism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg/330px-Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blond","wikidata":"Q202466"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/500px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=th